IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`
IMPORT `sgta-s2-definitions`
IMPORT `sgta-part8-penalties`
IMPORT `sgta-part9-general`
IMPORT `sgta-part6-offences`
IMPORT `sgta-ta-versions`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), REVISED EDITION 2000 (30 December 2000): ss 34, 35 and 36, the possession and operation offences and the exemption for treaty licences,
-- as they were numbered and worded in that Edition (TA1999.20001230.txt:1244-1287).  Their 2020 numbers are ss 54, 55 and 56 (sgta-part6-offences.l4).
-- Added 2026-11-04 on the independent review's gap G1: no module quoted the 2000 Edition's text of these sections, so the conduct days from 30 Dec 2000 to 15 May 2018 were answered from the
-- 2020 consolidation's words.  The words are the same except in drafting form ("shall be deemed" for "is deemed", "It shall be a defence" for "It is a defence", "No person shall" for
-- "A person must not", "dwelling-house" for "dwelling house"): the functions below therefore have the same bodies as the 2020 ones.
-- NO DEPOSITED ACT AMENDS THESE THREE SECTIONS: a search of Acts 10 of 2005, 19 of 2011, 22 of 2016, 30 of 2016 and 15 of 2017 for any amendment of section 34, 35 or 36 finds none, and the
-- 2020 consolidation prints their former numbers alone ("[34", "[35", "[36", TA1999.txt:4907, 4931, 4949) with no Act's number beside them.  So the Revised Edition 2000's words are the text printed
-- for every version of the Act from 30 Dec 2000 to the last deposited Act (Act 15 of 2017, in operation 23 May 2017; texts up to 15 May 2018).
-- WHAT IS NOT CHANGED: the outcome still names "section 54(2)" and "section 55(1)", the 2020 numbers, because the seat answers in the numbers of the Act as it is today; the 2000 Edition
-- numbers (34(2), 35(1)) are in the labels of these functions.  The penalty and the carve-out for broadcasting apparatus (2000 Ed. ss 65 and 72) are the version flags of
-- sgta-ta-versions.l4, as before.

§ `s 34 [2000 Edition] Prohibitions in respect of telecommunication and radio-communication equipment`

-- src:TA1999.20001230:1249 | (b) possess any radio-communication equipment,
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1250 | except and in accordance with a licence granted under section 5 or
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1251 | any regulations made under this Act.
@ref s 34(1) exception, 2000 Edition (src:TA1999.20001230:1249-1251)
GIVEN held IS A `What the person holds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person holds the licence or regulatory authority the exception names` MEANS
        held's `a licence granted under section 5`
    OR held's `an authorisation given by regulations made under this Act`

-- src:TA1999.20001230:1246 | 34.—(1) No person shall —
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1247 | (a) offer for sale, sell or possess for sale any telecommunication
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1248 | equipment; or
@ref s 34(1)(a), 2000 Edition (src:TA1999.20001230:1246-1248)
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
      `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` IS A BOOLEAN
      held IS A `What the person holds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(1)(a) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` MEANS
        `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it`
    AND `s 2: the equipment is used or intended to be used for telecommunications` e
    AND (NOT (`s 34(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person holds the licence or regulatory authority the exception names` held))

-- src:TA1999.20001230:1249 | (b) possess any radio-communication equipment,
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1250 | except and in accordance with a licence granted under section 5 or
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1251 | any regulations made under this Act.
@ref s 34(1)(b), 2000 Edition (src:TA1999.20001230:1249-1251)
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
      `the person possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      held IS A `What the person holds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(1)(b) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` MEANS
        `the person possesses it`
    AND `s 2 (composed): the equipment is radio-communication equipment` e
    AND (NOT (`s 34(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person holds the licence or regulatory authority the exception names` held))

-- src:TA1999.20001230:1252 | (2) Any person who contravenes or fails to comply with
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1253 | subsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 34(2), 2000 Edition (src:TA1999.20001230:1252-1253)
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
      `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      held IS A `What the person holds`
      `the question is the regulation of a telecommunication system required for the operation of a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is broadcasting apparatus as the Broadcasting Act 1994 defines it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Offence outcome`
`s 34(2) of the 2000 Edition: the outcome, on Reading A of s 72 (s 95 today)` MEANS
    IF     (   `s 34(1)(a) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` e `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` held
            OR `s 34(1)(b) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` e `the person possesses it` held)
       AND (NOT (held's `a licence issued in a treaty country and recognised under section 56`))
       AND (NOT (held's `an exemption given by the Minister under section 96`))
       AND (NOT (`s 95: the Act does not apply to the licensing of this apparatus` `the equipment is broadcasting apparatus as the Broadcasting Act 1994 defines it` `the question is the regulation of a telecommunication system required for the operation of a broadcasting service` FALSE))
    THEN `an offence under` "section 54(2)" (`s 85: the penalty for an offence under the Act` NOTHING)
    ELSE `no offence under this provision`

-- Reading B: the carve-out does not displace the offence.
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
      `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      held IS A `What the person holds`
GIVETH A `Offence outcome`
`s 34(2) of the 2000 Edition: the outcome, on Reading B of s 72 (s 95 today)` MEANS
    IF     (   `s 34(1)(a) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` e `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` held
            OR `s 34(1)(b) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` e `the person possesses it` held)
       AND (NOT (held's `a licence issued in a treaty country and recognised under section 56`))
       AND (NOT (held's `an exemption given by the Minister under section 96`))
    THEN `an offence under` "section 54(2)" (`s 85: the penalty for an offence under the Act` NOTHING)
    ELSE `no offence under this provision`

§ `s 35 [2000 Edition] Penalty for unlicensed station`

-- src:TA1999.20001230:1256 | 35.—(1) Any person who establishes, installs, maintains, provides
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1257 | or operates a radio-communication system or service or any radio-
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1258 | communication equipment in any place or on board any vessel,
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1259 | aircraft or in any vehicle in Singapore without a licence granted under
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1260 | section 5 or any regulations made under this Act shall be guilty of an
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1261 | offence.
@ref s 35(1), 2000 Edition (src:TA1999.20001230:1256-1261)
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
      `the person establishes, installs, maintains, provides or operates it, or a radio-communication system or service` IS A BOOLEAN
      where IS A `Where the equipment is`
      held IS A `What the person holds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
        `the person establishes, installs, maintains, provides or operates it, or a radio-communication system or service`
    AND `s 2 (composed): the equipment is radio-communication equipment` e
    AND (NOT (`s 34(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person holds the licence or regulatory authority the exception names` held))
    AND (NOT (held's `a licence issued in a treaty country and recognised under section 56`))
    AND (NOT (held's `an exemption given by the Minister under section 96`))

-- src:TA1999.20001230:1262 | (2) Any person who is in possession of any radio-communication
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1263 | equipment shall be deemed, until the contrary is proved, to have
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1264 | operated the same.
@ref s 35(2), 2000 Edition (src:TA1999.20001230:1262-1264)
GIVEN `the person is in possession of the radio-communication equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(2) of the 2000 Edition: the person is deemed to have operated it` MEANS
        `the person is in possession of the radio-communication equipment`
    AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)

-- src:TA1999.20001230:1270 | (3) The occupier of any dwelling-house or premises in which is
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1271 | installed any radio-communication equipment in respect of which a
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1272 | licence is not in force shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 35(3), 2000 Edition (src:TA1999.20001230:1270-1272)
GIVEN `the person is the occupier of a dwelling house or premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `radio-communication equipment is installed in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a licence is in force in respect of that equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(3) of the 2000 Edition: the occupier is guilty of an offence` MEANS
        `the person is the occupier of a dwelling house or premises`
    AND `radio-communication equipment is installed in it`
    AND (NOT `a licence is in force in respect of that equipment`)

-- src:TA1999.20001230:1273 | (4) It shall be a defence in any proceedings for an offence under
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1274 | subsection (3) that the occupier was not aware and could not with
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1275 | reasonable diligence have become aware of the existence in the
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1276 | dwelling-house or premises of the radio-communication equipment.
@ref s 35(4), 2000 Edition (src:TA1999.20001230:1273-1276)
GIVEN `the occupier was not aware` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occupier could not with reasonable diligence have become aware of the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(4) of the 2000 Edition: the defence is made out` MEANS
    `the occupier was not aware` AND `the occupier could not with reasonable diligence have become aware of the equipment`

§ `s 36 [2000 Edition] Exemption from sections 33, 34 and 35`

-- src:TA1999.20001230:1279 | 36. Subject to such conditions as the Authority may impose,
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1280 | sections 33, 34 and 35 shall not apply to any person who has been
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1281 | issued with a licence for the installation or working of any telecom-
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1282 | munication equipment under the provisions of any written law in
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1283 | force in any country which is a party to a treaty or any other
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1284 | arrangement to which Singapore is a party pursuant to which licences
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1285 | issued under the written laws in force in each country for the
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1286 | installation or working of any telecommunication equipment are
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1287 | recognised as having force in the other country.
@ref s 36, 2000 Edition (src:TA1999.20001230:1279-1287)
GIVEN `the person has been issued a licence for the installation or working of telecommunication equipment under the written law of a country that is party to a treaty or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under that treaty or arrangement such licences are recognised as having force in each country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36 of the 2000 Edition: sections 33, 34 and 35 do not apply to the person (subject to the Authority's conditions)` MEANS
        `the person has been issued a licence for the installation or working of telecommunication equipment under the written law of a country that is party to a treaty or arrangement`
    AND `under that treaty or arrangement such licences are recognised as having force in each country`

§ `The text of ss 34, 35 and 36 that each version of the Act prints`

-- Every deposited version up to Act 15 of 2017 prints the Revised Edition 2000's words (see the header); the version for the 2020 consolidation, and the row that stands for the Acts after
-- Act 15 of 2017 (whose own markers show no amendment of these sections), print the 2020 words.
GIVEN v IS AN `Act text version`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ss 34, 35 and 36 are printed in the words of the Revised Edition 2000 in the version` MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `Revised Edition 2000` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 10 of 2005` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 19 of 2011` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 22 of 2016` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 30 of 2016` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 15 of 2017` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Acts after Act 15 of 2017 that are not deposited` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the 2020 Revised Edition as deposited from SSO` THEN FALSE

GIVEN v IS AN `Act text version`
      e IS A `A piece of equipment`
      `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      held IS A `What the person holds`
      `the question is the regulation of a telecommunication system required for the operation of a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is broadcasting apparatus as the Broadcasting Act 1994 defines it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Offence outcome`
`s 34(2) or s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading A, in the text the version prints` MEANS
    IF `ss 34, 35 and 36 are printed in the words of the Revised Edition 2000 in the version` v
    THEN `s 34(2) of the 2000 Edition: the outcome, on Reading A of s 72 (s 95 today)` e `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` `the person possesses it` held `the question is the regulation of a telecommunication system required for the operation of a broadcasting service` `the equipment is broadcasting apparatus as the Broadcasting Act 1994 defines it`
    ELSE `s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading A of s 95` e `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` `the person possesses it` held `the question is the regulation of a telecommunication system required for the operation of a broadcasting service` `the equipment is broadcasting apparatus as the Broadcasting Act 1994 defines it`

GIVEN v IS AN `Act text version`
      e IS A `A piece of equipment`
      `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      held IS A `What the person holds`
GIVETH AN `Offence outcome`
`s 34(2) or s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading B, in the text the version prints` MEANS
    IF `ss 34, 35 and 36 are printed in the words of the Revised Edition 2000 in the version` v
    THEN `s 34(2) of the 2000 Edition: the outcome, on Reading B of s 72 (s 95 today)` e `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` `the person possesses it` held
    ELSE `s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading B of s 95` e `the person offers for sale, sells or possesses for sale it` `the person possesses it` held

GIVEN v IS AN `Act text version`
      e IS A `A piece of equipment`
      `the person establishes, installs, maintains, provides or operates it, or a radio-communication system or service` IS A BOOLEAN
      where IS A `Where the equipment is`
      held IS A `What the person holds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(1) or s 55(1): the person is guilty of an offence, in the text the version prints` MEANS
    IF `ss 34, 35 and 36 are printed in the words of the Revised Edition 2000 in the version` v
    THEN `s 35(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person is guilty of an offence` e `the person establishes, installs, maintains, provides or operates it, or a radio-communication system or service` where held
    ELSE `s 55(1): the person is guilty of an offence` e `the person establishes, installs, maintains, provides or operates it, or a radio-communication system or service` where held
